          "kicker": "Murrayfield defeat",
          "heading": "Ewan Ashman hat-trick not enough as Scotland fall 21-43 to New Zealand",
          "body": "Scotland failed to score after the interval as New Zealand pulled clear at Murrayfield on Saturday, leaving Ewan Ashman's first-half hat-trick as the home side's only bright spot. The All Blacks crossed seven times in all, two of them for Beauden Barrett, who beetled through Scotland's outside defences with ease. Their 19 unanswered second-half points followed, and the Guardian's match report called the result dispiritingly routine rather than one of the agonising defeats Scotland have suffered against them."
        },
