      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rivalry history",
          "heading": "Ieuan Evans scored inside 45 seconds in Wales' 1993 win over Japan",
          "body": "The first full capped match against Japan was a 1993 Cardiff afternoon, and Ieuan Evans, captaining Wales, was over in the right corner inside 45 seconds of kick-off. Japan's scrum-half threw a wild pass from a scrum, and Evans gathered the loose ball on the 10-metre line before racing clear. Evans says the early sprint strained his hamstrings, and Wales won convincingly. He later spoke Japanese at the post-match banquet, reading paragraphs written phonetically by Cardiff University's Business School."
        },
