      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Openside debate",
          "heading": "Jeff Wilson calls Peter Lakai world's best openside after Jacobson injury",
          "body": "Peter Lakai has moved to openside since injuries to Luke Jacobson and Ethan Blackadder opened the door, and he started the Nations Championship opener against Scotland alongside Wallace Sititi. Jeff Wilson, the former All Blacks star, repeated the claim on Sport Nation, saying: \"I think he's the best openside flanker in the world.\" He likened the Hurricanes loose forward to Michael Jones and called the 23-year-old an \"absolute superstar.\" New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 in that opener."
        },
