    "467": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Italy rout",
          "heading": "Feinberg-Mngomezulu scores 26 points as Springboks thrash Italy 66-7 in Turin",
          "body": "Six first-half tries gave the world champions a 45-0 lead at Allianz Stadium, and they finished with nine, Malcolm Marx scoring twice. Sacha Feinberg-Mngomezulu, who opened the scoring with a penalty, finished with 26 points against an Italy side missing 16 players through injury, including captain Michele Lamaro. Rassie Erasmus made a late change, Lood de Jager starting in place of Salmaan Moerat, who was set to make his first appearance of 2026. The bonus-point win protected South Africa's place at the top of the southern hemisphere log."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
